/*
Purple Telegram's own strings, in the format of lang.strings next to this
file. Upstream's lang.strings stays as upstream ships it: at build time
Telegram/cmake/purple_lang.cmake appends this file to it, and codegen_lang
reads the result, so tr:: works the same for these keys as for upstream's.

Add new Purple strings here, never to lang.strings. A key may not repeat one
of upstream's: codegen_lang stops with "duplicate found for key". See
docs/purple/upstream_hooks.md.
*/

